================================================================================
REFERENCED WORK
================================================================================

Consulted to understand Bedrock's formats and Bedrock/Java semantics. Where an
implementation here was informed by one of these, the source file says so and states
that the implementation is independent.

MIT — may be adapted with attribution:
    GeyserMC/Geyser, GeyserMC/mappings, GeyserMC/Hydraulic, GeyserMC/MCProtocolLib
        The largest existing body of Bedrock/Java semantic mappings.
    EaseCation/FabricRock
        The only prior attempt to load .mcaddon files in Java Edition.
    unnamed/hephaestus-engine, unnamed/creative

Apache-2.0 — may be adapted with attribution:
    CloudburstMC/Protocol

GPL-3.0 and AGPL-3.0 — READ ONLY. NO CODE FROM THESE IS PRESENT IN LEPUS:
    JannisX11/blockbench           the de-facto specification of the .geo.json format
    JannisX11/snowstorm            reference implementation of the particle format
    GeyserMC/Rainbow               its OUTPUT SCHEMA is matched; its code is not used
    Kas-tle/java2bedrock.sh
    CloudburstMC/Nukkit

    Reading a program to learn a FILE FORMAT is not derivation of that program.
    Reimplementing the format independently is legitimate, and the distinction is
    maintained deliberately: any file whose implementation was informed by one of
    these carries a comment naming what was consulted and asserting independence.
    If that cannot be stated honestly, the code does not go in.

LGPL-3.0 — consulted for component and AI semantics only:
    AllayMC/Allay, PowerNukkitX

